# Build context exclusions.
#
# The image build only consumes Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, src/, the reviewed validator inputs under
# container/, and the release license notices. These rules are defense-in-depth: an excluded file
# cannot be sent in the context or mounted at all, even if a future stage switches from a bind
# mount to COPY. Keep this list conservative; it must not exclude those inputs.

# Version-control metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Host build output and Rust artifacts (rebuilt inside the image)
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Generated feed output and validator caches (produced at runtime, never an input)
/out
/validation
/validation-reports
/.validator-cache

# Planning, security, and knowledge-graph directories
/.specs
/.security
/.superpowers
/.codebase-memory

# Documentation not needed to compile
/docs
*.md
!/LICENSE
!/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html
!/container/licenses/
!/container/licenses/**

# Container tooling itself
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Environment files, credentials, keys, and certificates
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Editor and OS artifacts
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*~
